[{:db/id "q-86483/selection/96f8d43800f3b6c20f84835923cad918ac060b7e1acd25b337ff3fc718f3017d" :answer/id #uuid "e8ede6a0-1e3d-5892-aa8d-c45b485c5304" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$4{e}^{t/2}$ cubic centimeters per hour" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86483/selection/bae7c0fe265593c4fb74f8cd6c4f971ed92d773317b416ff9bf70c7e04e20d33" :answer/id #uuid "a8e89c2c-795a-56a3-84e7-6374b983b768" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$8{e}^{2t}$ cubic centimeters per hour" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86483/selection/7dc24b297149482a604ff5499b05e6a2a337a81bcf1426ab2b817aa8a5a9a68d" :answer/id #uuid "c6a0656b-66e6-5f6e-baf6-d2208a9e7c63" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$8{e}^{t/2}$ cubic centimeters per hour" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86483/selection/364b0013263f3bc9799619456696c02331dbea5d0bd2c861c4a18e8f59364766" :answer/id #uuid "46de3614-09ff-5e05-825f-cb95073f4d3c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$4{e}^{2t}$ cubic centimeters per hour" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86483/selection/395bbb38cd006f2c08d731d188d0f545ab1bca953c7a37979f8091ef6252ede8" :answer/id #uuid "6125ba32-7495-55be-aa76-d2676bddfffd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$16{e}^{t/2}$ cubic centimeters per hour" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86483/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "38dbc5fe-ec62-5f64-98b8-52419e45ce5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-86483/selection/96f8d43800f3b6c20f84835923cad918ac060b7e1acd25b337ff3fc718f3017d" :answer-field/choices ["q-86483/selection/96f8d43800f3b6c20f84835923cad918ac060b7e1acd25b337ff3fc718f3017d" "q-86483/selection/bae7c0fe265593c4fb74f8cd6c4f971ed92d773317b416ff9bf70c7e04e20d33" "q-86483/selection/7dc24b297149482a604ff5499b05e6a2a337a81bcf1426ab2b817aa8a5a9a68d" "q-86483/selection/364b0013263f3bc9799619456696c02331dbea5d0bd2c861c4a18e8f59364766" "q-86483/selection/395bbb38cd006f2c08d731d188d0f545ab1bca953c7a37979f8091ef6252ede8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-86483" :question/id #uuid "a1cd418e-19aa-59f8-93b4-cb745f14ecef" :question/math-academy-id "q-86483" :question/problem "The function $v(t)=8{e}^{t/2}$ gives the volume, in cubic centimeters, of methylated spirit produced by a chemical process $t$ hours after the process begins. Find the instantaneous rate of change of spirit volume as a function of $t.$" :question/worked-solution "The instantaneous rate of change of the spirit volume is equal to ${v}^{′}(t).$\n\nNow, the rate of change of $v(t)$ with respect to $t$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8{e}^{t/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (8{e}^{t/2}) \\\\  & =4{e}^{t/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate change of the volume of spirit with respect to time is $4{e}^{t/2}$ cubic centimeters per hour." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-86483/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "236cec41-4836-5526-893d-e6f2a23d1801"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-86483"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-72357/selection/a0a28ce9a907d14a3c03cab1b98d65d15bfe8df40f6833ea9081ca6c57da1cd2" :answer/id #uuid "2a86e6bf-b123-54c8-ad39-b49fdd73e2ae" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{5}{9}$ degrees of Fahrenheit per degree of Celsius" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72357/selection/2ba1320a76cf9eedf57557daee654e3b5b16893243ae0fd371504492cb8c75ca" :answer/id #uuid "46ff578c-cac4-563d-8412-e9062ca9639f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{9}{5}$ degrees of Fahrenheit per degree of Celsius" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72357/selection/17f2a363c3d0a2fc3798ab00a4ba1fbb4582289e0bd3c8b0168cfce78b9c9e70" :answer/id #uuid "43329b9d-e113-5c0f-a41e-cfeead79d7b8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{169}{5}$ degrees of Fahrenheit per degree of Celsius" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72357/selection/4d084130d722bca1405e7462d22164af34344da0d2b45e2a271d6b5c9fad0d8e" :answer/id #uuid "a40460e7-1186-569b-b39c-95251f5fe61a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{293}{9}$ degrees of Fahrenheit per degree of Celsius" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72357/selection/3cfdab63d5e2860136f83ca8aeca784f446326dc60b827c686cb266f85ce7fd7" :answer/id #uuid "1c71d900-2229-5eea-a385-492c5d4668dc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{5}{169}$ degrees of Fahrenheit per degree of Celsius" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72357/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8b62f26e-2cfb-5faf-8c53-54f20df0dca0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-72357/selection/2ba1320a76cf9eedf57557daee654e3b5b16893243ae0fd371504492cb8c75ca" :answer-field/choices ["q-72357/selection/a0a28ce9a907d14a3c03cab1b98d65d15bfe8df40f6833ea9081ca6c57da1cd2" "q-72357/selection/2ba1320a76cf9eedf57557daee654e3b5b16893243ae0fd371504492cb8c75ca" "q-72357/selection/17f2a363c3d0a2fc3798ab00a4ba1fbb4582289e0bd3c8b0168cfce78b9c9e70" "q-72357/selection/4d084130d722bca1405e7462d22164af34344da0d2b45e2a271d6b5c9fad0d8e" "q-72357/selection/3cfdab63d5e2860136f83ca8aeca784f446326dc60b827c686cb266f85ce7fd7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-72357" :question/id #uuid "60bc5656-b32e-5701-901a-41c0c8fd54d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-72357" :question/problem "The air temperature $F$ in degrees Fahrenheit can be modeled by the function $F(C)=\\frac{9}{5}C+32,$ where $C$ is the air temperature in degrees Celsius. Find the instantaneous rate of change of the air temperature in degrees Fahrenheit with respect to the air temperature in degrees Celsius." :question/worked-solution "The instantaneous rate of change of the air temperature in degrees Fahrenheit with respect to the air temperature in degrees Celsius is equal to ${F}^{′}(C).$\n\nNow, the rate of change of $F(C)$ with respect to $C$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{′}(C) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}C}(\\frac{9}{5}C+32) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate change of the air temperature in degrees Fahrenheit with respect to the air temperature in degrees Celsius is $\\frac{9}{5}$ degrees Fahrenheit per degree of Celsius." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-72357/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "236cec41-4836-5526-893d-e6f2a23d1801"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72357"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-343166/field-1/24caf9c29d02d71aa60d28104b8806ae2ce94d762cdb5548695fc098942afbb0" :answer/id #uuid "9537d5e3-26d5-5698-96a6-c53109fc8e5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\ln(t+1)+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343166/field-1/b898b1fd0a104004694f1204ac82cf3afa7ef607739333fd25d3a1cec70fc748" :answer/id #uuid "b6934440-20a2-590b-a245-66e7f0a746d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\ln(t+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343166/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "12f72ab5-e1eb-5d08-8081-32ef946fbe1c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-343166/field-1/24caf9c29d02d71aa60d28104b8806ae2ce94d762cdb5548695fc098942afbb0" :answer-field/choices ["q-343166/field-1/24caf9c29d02d71aa60d28104b8806ae2ce94d762cdb5548695fc098942afbb0" "q-343166/field-1/b898b1fd0a104004694f1204ac82cf3afa7ef607739333fd25d3a1cec70fc748"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343166" :question/id #uuid "2e07b371-489a-5311-9833-37b80a53596c" :question/math-academy-id "q-343166" :question/problem "The funding $F,$ in millions of dollars, allocated to a research project $t$ years after it begins is modeled by\n\n$$\nF(t)=5+(t+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1),\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nWhat is the instantaneous rate of change of the funding as a function of $t?$\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change of the funding is\n{{field-1}} million dollars per year." :question/worked-solution "The instantaneous rate of change of the funding is ${F}^{′}(t).$\n\nWe take the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{d}{dt}[5+(t+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1)] \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1)+(t+1)\\cdot \\frac{1}{t+1} \\\\  & =1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change of the funding is $1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1)$ million dollars per year." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-343166/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "236cec41-4836-5526-893d-e6f2a23d1801"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343166"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-343167/field-1/95f753d3d588ccc445c6b9b2612032b87ac1449089ddb327c3289c8d4945fea8" :answer/id #uuid "9b79824f-0d58-561b-a13e-7f5242c46a7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2te^{-t}-t^2e^{-t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343167/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "956351f3-e5a9-506b-b875-9603998a6bb0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-343167/field-1/95f753d3d588ccc445c6b9b2612032b87ac1449089ddb327c3289c8d4945fea8" :answer-field/choices ["q-343167/field-1/95f753d3d588ccc445c6b9b2612032b87ac1449089ddb327c3289c8d4945fea8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343167" :question/id #uuid "3771af58-f6ea-5a0e-8fb6-883a58c8196f" :question/math-academy-id "q-343167" :question/problem "The inventory level $I,$ in hundreds of units, of a medical supply $t$ weeks after ordering begins, is modeled by\n\n$$\nI(t)={t}^{2}{e}^{-t}+12,\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nWhat is the instantaneous rate of change of the inventory level as a function of $t?$ \n\nThe instantaneous rate of change of the inventory level is\n{{field-1}} hundreds of units per week." :question/worked-solution "The instantaneous rate of change of the inventory level is ${I}^{′}(t).$\n\nWe take the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{d}{dt}[{t}^{2}{e}^{-t}+12] \\\\  & =2t{e}^{-t}+{t}^{2}\\cdot (-{e}^{-t}) \\\\  & =2t{e}^{-t}-{t}^{2}{e}^{-t} \\\\  & =t{e}^{-t}(2-t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change of the inventory level is $t{e}^{-t}(2-t)$ hundreds of units per week." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-343167/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "236cec41-4836-5526-893d-e6f2a23d1801"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343167"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-72356/selection/5c7416c98bc15bf055e8719043bfee26d5a0f5d24f143bf65bf592f54d811429" :answer/id #uuid "469086ff-5fd5-54a7-bfc0-faecc7f5c7e8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-50$ degrees Fahrenheit per minute" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72356/selection/9497c82c64526db8b626c97cb43ce1a94d0e6d91efd950b90fdec7fb710cc001" :answer/id #uuid "3deab803-29e9-5aac-b603-3c7f8f038bef" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-36$ degrees Fahrenheit per minute" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72356/selection/6d49473d5505b2d74862521f75f28f094d17818ef89966f461593dfbd8a33492" :answer/id #uuid "0381cefa-c2aa-56e1-8f37-1d69d183b280" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-108$ degrees Fahrenheit per minute" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72356/selection/646a83d88cdbbcb4a9b9d9aeae169a9dc1b7da33c02df254e5fc49afe0262b9a" :answer/id #uuid "566cf014-59dd-57f5-b3a0-7b04511b2e46" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-72$ degrees Fahrenheit per minute" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72356/selection/766992df293382495c360e7c4fb09e18e910138bd80f9230022af86f669fb2b9" :answer/id #uuid "02baa62e-d511-5d50-846b-133b571bc3b2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-54$ degrees Fahrenheit per minute" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72356/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bad2a0a6-bc28-5701-b465-2fb9a735e0eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-72356/selection/6d49473d5505b2d74862521f75f28f094d17818ef89966f461593dfbd8a33492" :answer-field/choices ["q-72356/selection/5c7416c98bc15bf055e8719043bfee26d5a0f5d24f143bf65bf592f54d811429" "q-72356/selection/9497c82c64526db8b626c97cb43ce1a94d0e6d91efd950b90fdec7fb710cc001" "q-72356/selection/6d49473d5505b2d74862521f75f28f094d17818ef89966f461593dfbd8a33492" "q-72356/selection/646a83d88cdbbcb4a9b9d9aeae169a9dc1b7da33c02df254e5fc49afe0262b9a" "q-72356/selection/766992df293382495c360e7c4fb09e18e910138bd80f9230022af86f669fb2b9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-72356" :question/id #uuid "af3a3dc0-c338-5ee0-b1a3-cea63f01a521" :question/math-academy-id "q-72356" :question/problem "The temperature, in degrees Fahrenheit, of a rapidly cooling substance after $t$ minutes can be modeled by the function $F(t)=250-{t}^{3}.$ Find the instantaneous rate at which the temperature of the substance is changing with respect to time at the moment when the temperature of the substance is equal to $34$ degrees Fahrenheit." :question/worked-solution "Since we are given that the temperature of the substance is $34$ degrees Fahrenheit, the time can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}34 & =250-{t}^{3} \\\\ {t}^{3} & =216 \\\\ t & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe instantaneous rate at which the temperature of the substance is changing when $t=6$ minutes is equal to ${F}^{′}(6).$\n\nTaking the derivative, the rate of change of $F(t)$ with respect to $t$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(250-{t}^{3})=-3{t}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand evaluating at $t=6$ gives\n\n$$\n{F}^{′}(6)=-3(6)^{2}=-108.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate at which the temperature of the substance is changing when $t=6$ minutes is $-108$ degrees Fahrenheit per minute." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-72356/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff5ec0b-1456-5231-94e1-0fc5923d6672"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72356"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186260569 :question/answer-fields 17592186274750] {:db/id "q-48700/selection/ma-v1/37572fa21c4bd46f5e5c92a60937590fb278245c43424d84fff9bb97fabcca6f/4c3047c1aee66c6413a32aae9d29a3ab61accf7247ed98a01b2867c18b54a35d" :answer/id #uuid "dc73284c-f8d5-5ff3-b9bd-96d45f3598be" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1\\,495$ computers per day" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48700/selection/ma-v1/37572fa21c4bd46f5e5c92a60937590fb278245c43424d84fff9bb97fabcca6f/88f5e79a89cd940220c95c2d4f468fd0e7d14b3d1b6c02f351b715848d362a95" :answer/id #uuid "e0cc9bae-b4a6-56f2-8dd2-682f8c8008c6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1\\,801$ computers per day" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48700/selection/ma-v1/37572fa21c4bd46f5e5c92a60937590fb278245c43424d84fff9bb97fabcca6f/1b6145080ee3de6f0cbdc067912754ea206a53febdb85c99d928040468caad72" :answer/id #uuid "b02029e3-c2e5-5cae-8e1e-987d224a052d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1\\,699$ computers per day" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48700/selection/ma-v1/37572fa21c4bd46f5e5c92a60937590fb278245c43424d84fff9bb97fabcca6f/118bdbfd8aa93b8efce414d73281296ef6c3e913c2917b2b234d51fe942bdae7" :answer/id #uuid "9302bc57-0b92-57ac-ac8a-40346871ae5f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1\\,695$ computers per day" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48700/selection/ma-v1/37572fa21c4bd46f5e5c92a60937590fb278245c43424d84fff9bb97fabcca6f/5d77b89be4408aaba812104b275f2e175d23307f96851d34bf4470a6f1c401e3" :answer/id #uuid "53d48ccb-79d3-5295-9847-af807c0197c6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1\\,501$ computers per day" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48700/selection/ma-v1/37572fa21c4bd46f5e5c92a60937590fb278245c43424d84fff9bb97fabcca6f" :answer-field/id #uuid "b314822c-8502-5d9c-96db-55ae51a7bb14" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-48700/selection/ma-v1/37572fa21c4bd46f5e5c92a60937590fb278245c43424d84fff9bb97fabcca6f/1b6145080ee3de6f0cbdc067912754ea206a53febdb85c99d928040468caad72" :answer-field/choices ["q-48700/selection/ma-v1/37572fa21c4bd46f5e5c92a60937590fb278245c43424d84fff9bb97fabcca6f/4c3047c1aee66c6413a32aae9d29a3ab61accf7247ed98a01b2867c18b54a35d" "q-48700/selection/ma-v1/37572fa21c4bd46f5e5c92a60937590fb278245c43424d84fff9bb97fabcca6f/88f5e79a89cd940220c95c2d4f468fd0e7d14b3d1b6c02f351b715848d362a95" "q-48700/selection/ma-v1/37572fa21c4bd46f5e5c92a60937590fb278245c43424d84fff9bb97fabcca6f/1b6145080ee3de6f0cbdc067912754ea206a53febdb85c99d928040468caad72" "q-48700/selection/ma-v1/37572fa21c4bd46f5e5c92a60937590fb278245c43424d84fff9bb97fabcca6f/118bdbfd8aa93b8efce414d73281296ef6c3e913c2917b2b234d51fe942bdae7" "q-48700/selection/ma-v1/37572fa21c4bd46f5e5c92a60937590fb278245c43424d84fff9bb97fabcca6f/5d77b89be4408aaba812104b275f2e175d23307f96851d34bf4470a6f1c401e3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-48700"] :question/worked-solution "The instantaneous rate of change in the spread when $t=9$ days is equal to ${f}^{′}(9).$ \n\nFirst, we take the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{100\\,({t}^{3}+2)}{t+1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{100(3{t}^{2})(t+1)-100({t}^{3}+2)(1)}{{(t+1)}^{2}} \\\\  & =100\\cdot \\frac{2{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}-2}{{(t+1)}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $t=9,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(9) & =100\\cdot \\frac{2(9)^{3}+3(9)^{2}-2}{{((9)+1)}^{2}} \\\\  & =100\\cdot \\frac{1\\,458+243-2}{100} \\\\  & =1\\,699.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change in the spread when $t=9$ is $1\\,699$ computers per day." :question/answer-fields ["q-48700/selection/ma-v1/37572fa21c4bd46f5e5c92a60937590fb278245c43424d84fff9bb97fabcca6f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-72367/selection/09e75dbd0a3683df62875cace492d8e8f943664ac1126762c85c3f75dca5ad31" :answer/id #uuid "26ce2d59-0559-5532-b34b-752dc89fae5b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-9{e}^{-3}$ liters per dollar" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72367/selection/5e1eef5c77339d9355b9a72205eaedde29886f097b59499ae713a4ffd99aa5ed" :answer/id #uuid "65c7cc0f-e99c-5b77-9062-0b10f09a6dd4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-12{e}^{-9}$ liters per dollar" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72367/selection/560cd03ff0c4c67481000cb9ca3d90cef8c3e4f27d4f941aa1d5db27a52a688c" :answer/id #uuid "6a286758-9831-5d20-a330-8972dda43713" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-10e$ liters per dollar" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72367/selection/d3515b085c6ab67d98326ad1ce2cc5951756430a3c6121785fa7cde56a31cbcf" :answer/id #uuid "ea27b3f0-cf48-516c-86e4-2d58d94865fd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-8{e}^{-9}$ liters per dollar" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72367/selection/ddaa92c3e1960e39c862eb9fa09be1eeacef470107eb0b04a92fa701cc6305c1" :answer/id #uuid "bc09f5e2-b539-5e88-960a-7ec85bfdb99e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-6{e}^{9}$ liters per dollar" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72367/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "99c25c86-8a1b-5f85-9930-bc19be1e7305" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-72367/selection/5e1eef5c77339d9355b9a72205eaedde29886f097b59499ae713a4ffd99aa5ed" :answer-field/choices ["q-72367/selection/09e75dbd0a3683df62875cace492d8e8f943664ac1126762c85c3f75dca5ad31" "q-72367/selection/5e1eef5c77339d9355b9a72205eaedde29886f097b59499ae713a4ffd99aa5ed" "q-72367/selection/560cd03ff0c4c67481000cb9ca3d90cef8c3e4f27d4f941aa1d5db27a52a688c" "q-72367/selection/d3515b085c6ab67d98326ad1ce2cc5951756430a3c6121785fa7cde56a31cbcf" "q-72367/selection/ddaa92c3e1960e39c862eb9fa09be1eeacef470107eb0b04a92fa701cc6305c1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-72367" :question/id #uuid "eedc7cd2-9ab3-5727-ada2-18fc9f2156b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-72367" :question/problem "The function $g(p)={e}^{-4{p}^{2}}$ models the volume of gas that a vendor can sell, in liters, at a price of $p$ dollars per liter. Find the instantaneous rate at which the volume of gas is changing with respect to the price when $p=1.50$ dollars." :question/worked-solution "The instantaneous rate at which the volume of gas that can be sold is changing when $p=1.50$ dollars is equal to ${g}^{′}(1.5).$\n\nTaking the derivative, the rate of change of $g(p)$ with respect to $p$ is \n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(p)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}p}({e}^{-4{p}^{2}})=-8p{e}^{-4{p}^{2}},\n$$\n\nand evaluating at $p=1.5$ gives\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(1.5)=-8(1.5){e}^{-4(1.5)^{2}}=-12{e}^{-9}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate at which the volume of gas that can be sold is changing when $p=1.5$ dollars is $-12{e}^{-9}$ liters per dollar." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-72367/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff5ec0b-1456-5231-94e1-0fc5923d6672"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72367"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-343498/field-1/1be980d47b7c8688003a0125c366085994673fb630263e0102cd536ae08b007a" :answer/id #uuid "c9d523ba-9b37-5749-9a36-a7981cff36a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "40\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343498/field-1/52964da0f06458a16fef4782c5b89ddeb65c5acad01baca0884b33117060e88f" :answer/id #uuid "8bc9dae0-08fc-5a43-9634-6a5ab6bd891b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "100\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-343498/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "13cf4b10-a598-5e0e-921f-502564520d45" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-343498/field-1/1be980d47b7c8688003a0125c366085994673fb630263e0102cd536ae08b007a" :answer-field/choices ["q-343498/field-1/1be980d47b7c8688003a0125c366085994673fb630263e0102cd536ae08b007a" "q-343498/field-1/52964da0f06458a16fef4782c5b89ddeb65c5acad01baca0884b33117060e88f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-343498" :question/id #uuid "507d7e12-bec8-5924-a111-bf667b784658" :question/math-academy-id "q-343498" :question/problem "The surface area $A$ of a sphere is increasing. Find the instantaneous rate at which the surface area of the sphere is changing with respect to its radius at the moment when the radius of the sphere is equal to $5\\,\\text{in}.$\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change at the moment when its radius is $5$ inches is equal to\n{{field-1}} ${\\text{in}}^{2}/\\text{in}.$" :question/worked-solution "We know that the surface area of a sphere with radius $r$ is given by \n\n$$\nA=A(r)=4\\pi {r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTaking the derivative, the rate of change of $A(r)$ with respect to $r$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{′}(r) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}r}(4\\pi {r}^{2}) \\\\  & =4\\pi (2r) \\\\  & =8\\pi r,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand evaluating at $r=5$ gives\n\n$$\n{A}^{′}(5)=8\\pi (5)=40\\pi .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate at which the surface area of the sphere is changing when its radius is $5\\,\\text{in}$, is $40\\pi $ ${\\text{in}}^{2}/\\text{in}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-343498/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "20b289d4-96a7-5d1b-9714-6afabab4804d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-343498"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186259051 :question/answer-fields 17592186274589] {:db/id "q-2545/selection/ma-v1/234335b60ad7538053ed9d53dffd800dcc298e509d2ecc34f55b47daccc0336e/5fc5100246d98d57a3a3e1d40181b00e6e8dff5d4a097ce2d7b7f6ae0b08578e" :answer/id #uuid "8c248248-84d5-57d4-b6ce-fe4a85f98373" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2545/selection/ma-v1/234335b60ad7538053ed9d53dffd800dcc298e509d2ecc34f55b47daccc0336e/b72c171200f2b266c61622fd6538cf026085a2a1fc0c612bfb7e1deff0c4c572" :answer/id #uuid "e78e8e43-abd8-5cf1-8c86-fd1003f57849" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "C\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2545/selection/ma-v1/234335b60ad7538053ed9d53dffd800dcc298e509d2ecc34f55b47daccc0336e/63dd0b7ef0f26edc7e822cf913c17712483e1cf624bbd0197240a53f0f7176a3" :answer/id #uuid "7fcbd2af-f496-5ae2-aff8-1c1a8c03dcfd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{C}{2\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2545/selection/ma-v1/234335b60ad7538053ed9d53dffd800dcc298e509d2ecc34f55b47daccc0336e/3be9bb237d805d834da5bcacae0d847c741b9a112b0c553382f2d89f0f26f368" :answer/id #uuid "838cf9ad-6de2-55f4-a99c-8657f56e70ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{C}{4\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2545/selection/ma-v1/234335b60ad7538053ed9d53dffd800dcc298e509d2ecc34f55b47daccc0336e/aa06573b28e00764609c16dd3ba54f9340aecbf73789f129f8540a508cef1fa2" :answer/id #uuid "2e8e9cc9-632f-59bf-914f-6bcbd2efd7d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2C}{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2545/selection/ma-v1/234335b60ad7538053ed9d53dffd800dcc298e509d2ecc34f55b47daccc0336e" :answer-field/id #uuid "316d79eb-c7b6-5349-bbfa-8d92c0c4eeba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-2545/selection/ma-v1/234335b60ad7538053ed9d53dffd800dcc298e509d2ecc34f55b47daccc0336e/63dd0b7ef0f26edc7e822cf913c17712483e1cf624bbd0197240a53f0f7176a3" :answer-field/choices ["q-2545/selection/ma-v1/234335b60ad7538053ed9d53dffd800dcc298e509d2ecc34f55b47daccc0336e/5fc5100246d98d57a3a3e1d40181b00e6e8dff5d4a097ce2d7b7f6ae0b08578e" "q-2545/selection/ma-v1/234335b60ad7538053ed9d53dffd800dcc298e509d2ecc34f55b47daccc0336e/b72c171200f2b266c61622fd6538cf026085a2a1fc0c612bfb7e1deff0c4c572" "q-2545/selection/ma-v1/234335b60ad7538053ed9d53dffd800dcc298e509d2ecc34f55b47daccc0336e/63dd0b7ef0f26edc7e822cf913c17712483e1cf624bbd0197240a53f0f7176a3" "q-2545/selection/ma-v1/234335b60ad7538053ed9d53dffd800dcc298e509d2ecc34f55b47daccc0336e/3be9bb237d805d834da5bcacae0d847c741b9a112b0c553382f2d89f0f26f368" "q-2545/selection/ma-v1/234335b60ad7538053ed9d53dffd800dcc298e509d2ecc34f55b47daccc0336e/aa06573b28e00764609c16dd3ba54f9340aecbf73789f129f8540a508cef1fa2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-2545"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037675/assets/f59f65e184ccf4fdf2ae2124543ece45d41afce09d743dec9f17730dd00124d4.png)\n\nThe area $A$ of the circle above is increasing. The circumference and radius of the circle are $C$ and $r$ respectively. \nFind the rate of change of the area of the circle with respect to its circumference." :question/worked-solution "The area of a circle is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\pi {r}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the circle.\n\nWe know that $C=2\\pi r.$ so we can express the area $A$ as a function of the circumference $C$ by substituting $r=\\frac{C}{2\\pi }$ in the formula above. We get\n\n$$\nA=\\pi {r}^{2}=\\pi {(\\frac{C}{2\\pi })}^{2}=\\frac{{C}^{2}}{4\\pi }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $A(C)$ with respect to $C$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{′}(C) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}C}(\\frac{{C}^{2}}{4\\pi }) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\pi }\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}C}({C}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\pi }(2C) \\\\  & =\\frac{C}{2\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/answer-fields ["q-2545/selection/ma-v1/234335b60ad7538053ed9d53dffd800dcc298e509d2ecc34f55b47daccc0336e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-343502/field-1/851394d2ff5396d7e98d6942b438433571014ed5c3b562e88f0e9d335f210589" :answer/id #uuid "c48d34f1-d84d-51c7-96b0-c287ce05a6d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1000" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186266167 :answer-field/choices ["q-343502/field-1/851394d2ff5396d7e98d6942b438433571014ed5c3b562e88f0e9d335f210589"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-343502"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037675/assets/5fc1aff711355a147abac33a513434c55575c552ab58f0164ebc87222530f371.png)\n\nThe volume of a cube-shaped container is increasing. Find the instantaneous rate at which the volume of the container is changing with respect to the side length at the moment when the face diagonal of the cube is equal to $10\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{cm}.$\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change at the moment when the face diagonal is $10\\sqrt{2}$ centimeters is equal to\n{{field-1}} ${\\text{cm}}^{3}/\\text{cm}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-48728/selection/d4c281da4972f48e32ba81870d014d10d0f7a7e24d11e04a1d303808f210a4f8" :answer/id #uuid "ed587da6-042b-5ee8-852e-c07fb7353538" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "300\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}/\\text{cm}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48728/selection/04f53e43a01df4e9e02aad470ac27deef069b6f14cd4600bb2f3c9e149eb25b0" :answer/id #uuid "b3b19f6b-d5db-5615-bdec-a86c99773854" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "400\\pi \\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}/\\text{cm}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48728/selection/578324483f3716645dc56249c62d4be533181426551fc43c19dd198b63d8072a" :answer/id #uuid "0c2cc91f-1d24-59d8-8e2f-34d800d495e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,600\\pi \\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}/\\text{cm}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48728/selection/c6e365b6cad330de326ace6c380828315efc0fa7eaa24692ed5ffb258bb4208b" :answer/id #uuid "6404aa9b-f9e2-5e42-b886-2a1142be79e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "400\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}/\\text{cm}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48728/selection/90592c00ce0d9b11e31444511b4a5e710496476ad4370ea056226ae6d34a5a9a" :answer/id #uuid "f2443660-7bd3-5940-b5e3-362e8ac4ce51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "300\\pi \\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}/\\text{cm}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48728/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b395a869-7c8e-5438-8347-1bdf9c83021e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-48728/selection/04f53e43a01df4e9e02aad470ac27deef069b6f14cd4600bb2f3c9e149eb25b0" :answer-field/choices ["q-48728/selection/d4c281da4972f48e32ba81870d014d10d0f7a7e24d11e04a1d303808f210a4f8" "q-48728/selection/04f53e43a01df4e9e02aad470ac27deef069b6f14cd4600bb2f3c9e149eb25b0" "q-48728/selection/578324483f3716645dc56249c62d4be533181426551fc43c19dd198b63d8072a" "q-48728/selection/c6e365b6cad330de326ace6c380828315efc0fa7eaa24692ed5ffb258bb4208b" "q-48728/selection/90592c00ce0d9b11e31444511b4a5e710496476ad4370ea056226ae6d34a5a9a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-48728" :question/id #uuid "0340e2b4-a8dc-5b2e-8637-96bee21fbe98" :question/math-academy-id "q-48728" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037675/assets/d56c10dfa022454135ddafd4255f737182bdca186b99ed1e686132447341bff8.png)\n\nA spherical balloon is being inflated so that its volume is increasing. Find the instantaneous rate at which the volume of the balloon is changing with respect to the radius at the moment when the diameter of the balloon is equal to $20\\,\\text{cm}.$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given that the diameter of the spherical balloon is $20\\,\\text{cm}$,  its radius $r$ is $10\\,\\text{cm}.$ Now, the volume of a sphere with radius $r$  is given by \n\n$$\nV=V(r)=\\frac{4}{3}\\pi {r}^{3}.\n$$\n\nTaking the derivative, the rate of change of $V(r)$ with respect to $r$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{V}^{′}(r) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}r}(\\frac{4}{3}\\pi {r}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\pi (3{r}^{2}) \\\\  & =4\\pi {r}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand evaluating at $r=10$ gives\n\n$$\n{V}^{′}(10)=4\\pi (10)^{2}=400\\pi .\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the instantaneous rate at which the volume of the balloon is increasing when the diameter is $20\\,\\text{cm}$ is $400\\pi \\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}/\\text{cm}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-48728/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "20b289d4-96a7-5d1b-9714-6afabab4804d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48728"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6174"] :question/problem "A particle moves in a straight line. After $t$ seconds the particle is $\\, f(t)=2t^3 - 5t + 9\\,$ feet away from its initial position. What is the instantaneous rate of change of the particle's position as a function of $t?$" :question/worked-solution "The instantaneous rate of change of the particle's position is equal to $f'(t).$ \n\nWe take the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3}-5t+9) \\\\  & =6{t}^{2}-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $t$ seconds, the instantaneous rate of change of the particle's position is $6t^2 - 5$ feet per second." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-276"] :question/problem "Lizzie buys $b$ pounds of bananas at a price $p,$ in dollars, that can be modeled by the function $p(b)=5e^{-0.2b}.$ What is the instantaneous rate of change of the price when $b=5$ pounds?" :question/worked-solution "The instantaneous rate of change of the price when $b=5$ pounds is equal to $p'(5).$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}^{′}(b) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}b}(5{e}^{-0.2b}) \\\\  & =5{e}^{-0.2b}\\cdot (-0.2) \\\\  & =-{e}^{-0.2b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $b=5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}^{′}(5) & =-{e}^{-0.2(5)} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{e}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate change of the price when $b=5$ pounds is $-\\dfrac{1}{e}$ dollars per pound." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-275"] :question/problem "A spherical balloon is being inflated so that its volume is increasing. Find the instantaneous rate at which the volume of the balloon is changing with respect to the radius at the moment when the diameter of the balloon is equal to $12\\, \\text{cm}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037675/assets/e03fb046f74771676d7b1e83a1cf09176adcffaf8112e9de263404b8be74b026.png)" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given that the diameter of the balloon is $12\\, \\text{cm},$ its radius is $r =6\\, \\text{cm}.$ Now, we know that the volume of a sphere with radius $r$  is given by \n\n$$\nV= V(r) = \\dfrac{4}{3}\\pi r^3.\n$$\n\nTaking the derivative, the rate of change of $V(r)$  with respect to $r$ is \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\nV'(r) &= \\dfrac{\\textrm d }{\\textrm d r}\\left(  \\dfrac{4}{3}\\pi r^3\\right)\\[5pt]\n &  =  \\dfrac{4}{3}\\pi (3r^2)\\[5pt]\n &= 4\\pi r^2, \n}\n$$\n\nand evaluating at $r=6$ gives\n\n$$\nV'(6)=  4\\pi (6)^2= 144\\pi.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate at which the volume of the balloon is changing when its diameter is $12\\, \\text{cm}\\,$ is $\\, 144\\pi \\, \\text{cm}^3/\\text{cm}.$\n\n**Note:** We read $\\text{cm}^3/\\text{cm}$ as \"centimeters cubed per centimeter\"." :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
